factor-base64
=============

Base64 encoder and decoder for files, written in Factor.

* encodes any file to base64
* decodes base64 back to the original bytes
* pads the last group with =
* output is a single line, no wrapping
* whitespace in the input is ignored when decoding

Usage
-----

Run it from the repository root:

	factor -roots=src -run=b64 encode|decode <file>

Encode a file and save the result:

	factor -roots=src -run=b64 encode hello.txt > hello.b64

Decode it back:

	factor -roots=src -run=b64 decode hello.b64

Example output:

	aGVsbG8K
	hello

Use the words from the listener:

	USE: b64
	"hello" >base64 print
	"aGVsbG8=" base64> .
